  "identifier": "totalsegmentator",
  "name": "TotalSegmentator",
  "description": "Automated segmentation of more than 100 anatomical structures in CT and MR images using nnU-Net-based models. Covers bones, muscles, organs, vessels, and vertebrae in a single command. Widely used for clinical research workflows requiring rapid, reproducible whole-body or region-specific anatomical segmentation without manual labelling. Published in Radiology: Artificial Intelligence. Developed at University Hospital Basel.",
  "url": "https://github.com/wasserth/TotalSegmentator",
