  "mach:judgement": "Adopt",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The go-to tool for automated whole-body anatomical segmentation in CT and MR. 2,680 stars and 427 forks make it one of the most adopted medical imaging tools on GitHub. Apache-2.0, pip-installable, runs in a single command. Built on nnU-Net, covering 100+ structures including bones, organs, muscles, and vessels. Published in Radiology: Artificial Intelligence. Actively maintained through May 2026. Essential for any team needing reproducible anatomical segmentation for clinical research, radiomics, or surgical planning — and the default choice before considering custom segmentation model training.",
